QEMU/KVM UEFI boot evidence; no physical disk attached.

Fallback-only menu:
With other UKI candidates isolated in the disposable overlay, menu displayed only the previous-production fallback entry and its countdown selected it.

The disposable copy-on-write overlay was based on target-boot.qcow2. This boot intentionally stopped at the LUKS2 prompt; no passphrase was entered because the disposable test key had been removed. This proves menu selection and UKI/initramfs reached encrypted-root unlock, not unlock or userspace login.

